LC 242 — Valid Anagram
Pattern:Hashing

Logic:
Count how many times each character appears in both strings.
If all counts match → anagram.

Algorithm:
Count characters in s
Subtract characters using t
If all counts = 0 → true

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    bool isAnagram(string s, string t) {
        if (s.size() != t.size())
            return false;

        int count[26] = {};

        for (char c : s)
            count[c - 'a']++;

        for (char c : t)
            count[c - 'a']--;

        for (int x : count)
            if (x != 0)
                return false;

        return true;
    }
};

EX:
s = "anagram"
t = "nagaram"

a → 3 in both
n → 1 in both
g → 1 in both
r → 1 in both
m → 1 in both

All counts match
Answer = true ✅

Complexity:

Time: O(n)
Space: O(1)
